From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:30:48 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 73/92] drm/panel: add Samsung EA8061S panel driver

Driver for the 720x1280 AMOLED video mode DSI panel of the Galaxy J4,
ported from the vendor driver: power sequencing, the init and display-on
sequences, the MTP calibration read and the dynamic AID gamma tables behind
a backlight device.

The calibration reads set the maximum return packet size first, as the
panel answers with a single byte otherwise, and the init sequence applies
the brightness without taking the panel lock, which prepare() already
holds.

If the bootloader left the panel running with its video stream up
(samsung,keep-bootloader-state), the first prepare() does not power-cycle
or re-initialise it.

Signed-off-by: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit d2c5c6810f273e9f0b99f76064dbb89625cbd3fc)
